---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const lastUpdated = 'June 22, 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Voxivium"
  description="How Voxivium collects, uses, shares, and protects your information across our website and the Voxivium app."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/legal/privacy' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="legal">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        <p class="lead">
          This policy describes the personal information Voxivium collects, how it is used, with
          whom it may be shared, and the rights you have with respect to that information.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="prose">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This policy covers <strong>voxivium.com</strong> (the website you're reading) and the
          <strong>Voxivium app</strong> . When we say "Voxivium," "we," "us," or "our," we mean 
          Voxivium, PBC, a Delaware Public Benefit Corporation. When we say "you," we mean a 
          visitor to our website or a user of our app.
        </p>
        <p>
          Voxivium is available to citizens of the United States who are at least 18 years of age
          and who are registered to vote in the United States. Eligibility is confirmed through
          the identity verification and voter registration verification processes described below.
        </p>

        <h2>The information we collect</h2>

        <h3>From visitors to voxivium.com</h3>
        <p>
          The marketing site collects only what you give us. If you fill out one of our interest
          forms (voter signup, politician inquiry, media or research inquiry, AI lab inquiry), we
          collect the fields you submit—typically your name, email address, and a small set of
          context fields specific to your audience, such as your organization, jurisdiction, or
          intended use case.
        </p>
        <p>
          Beyond that, we use Cloudflare Web Analytics for basic, privacy-respecting traffic
          measurement. Cloudflare Web Analytics does not use cookies and does not fingerprint
          visitors. We do not run Google Analytics, the Meta pixel, or any third-party advertising
          trackers on this site.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site stores your color-theme preference (light or dark) in your browser's
          <code>localStorage</code>. This preference is stored locally and is not transmitted to
          Voxivium.
        </p>

        <h3>From users of the Voxivium app</h3>
        <p>
          Creating and maintaining a Voxivium voter account involves the following categories of
          information:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Account information.</strong> Your email address. Authentication is handled
            by Google Firebase Authentication, which manages credentials on Voxivium's behalf.
            You may register and sign in either by setting a password or by using a third-party
            sign-in provider (Sign in with Google or Sign in with Apple). Where you set a
            password, your password is transmitted to Firebase Authentication at the time of
            sign-in or registration; Voxivium does not store your password, in any form, and does
            not have access to your plaintext password. Where you use a third-party sign-in
            provider, that provider authenticates you and transmits to Voxivium a limited set of
            information consisting of your email address — or, if you use Sign in with Apple's
            private email relay, a relay email address — and a unique account identifier. Voxivium
            does not receive the password for, or any other credentials to, your account with that
            provider.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Identity verification data.</strong> When you complete identity verification,
            Voxivium transmits the personal details required by its third-party identity
            verification provider (such as full legal name, date of birth, and address) to that
            provider for the purpose of verifying your identity. Voxivium does not collect or
            store your government-issued identity documents. Voxivium retains only the
            verification result and the data necessary to operate the service (see Profile data,
            below).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Voter registration verification.</strong> We use a third-party
            voter-registration verification service to confirm that you are a U.S. registered
            voter. From that check, we store only your <strong>registration status</strong> and
            your <strong>assigned voter districts</strong> (federal, state, and local). We do not
            collect or store your voting history.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Profile data.</strong> Your real first name and last name, residential
            address, date of birth, political party affiliation, gender, voter districts, and—only
            if you choose to provide it—your race or ethnicity.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Civic input.</strong> Your stated stances and importance ratings on beliefs,
            your responses to polls, and your stances on specific pieces of legislation, executive
            orders, and court rulings.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Payment information.</strong> Subscriptions and other purchases made through
            the Voxivium mobile application on iOS are processed by Apple, and on Android by
            Google, in each case subject to those providers' terms and privacy policies.
            Subscriptions and other purchases made through the Voxivium website are processed by
            our third-party payment processor. Voxivium does not store full payment card numbers;
            it receives only the limited transaction metadata required to manage your account and
            subscription.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Technical and security data.</strong> When you access Voxivium, our servers
            and infrastructure providers automatically receive certain technical information,
            including IP address, device type, operating system, application or browser version,
            and timestamps of access. This information is used solely to operate the service
            securely and reliably, including for authentication, rate limiting, abuse and fraud
            prevention, error diagnosis, and determining application version compatibility. It is
            not used for advertising or behavioral profiling.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Notification preferences.</strong> Your settings for push, email, and in-app
            notifications.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>To operate the service.</strong> Generating your personal accountability scorecards,
            candidate comparisons, polls, and notifications requires the information described
            above.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To keep your records current.</strong> We periodically re-check your voter
            registration status (typically quarterly) so that your assigned representatives and
            districts stay accurate, and to detect changes such as a move or a registration lapse.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To produce aggregated, anonymized insights.</strong> The civic data you
            provide is the foundation of the aggregated, anonymized statistics we share with paid
            customers (politicians, media, researchers, AI labs)—described below.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To communicate with you.</strong> Service announcements, security alerts, and
            notifications you've opted into.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To improve and secure the service.</strong> Diagnostic data, abuse detection,
            and standard product analytics.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To comply with the law.</strong> Where we are legally required to retain or
            disclose information.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we share your information</h2>

        <h3>What we will never sell or share</h3>
        <p>
          Voxivium will <strong
            >never sell or share your personally identifiable information</strong
          >, including your name, residential address, date of birth, email address, or phone
          number. That commitment is part of the platform's design and is reflected in our
          corporate bylaws.
        </p>

        <h3>What we may share, only as aggregated and anonymized data</h3>
        <p>
          To paid customers (politicians, media organizations, academic researchers, and AI labs),
          Voxivium may share <strong>aggregated, anonymized</strong> data derived from the
          following categories:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Political party affiliation</li>
          <li>Gender</li>
          <li>Race or ethnicity (only where you have voluntarily provided it)</li>
          <li>Belief stances and importance ratings</li>
          <li>Polling responses</li>
          <li>Stances on specific issues, legislation, court rulings, and executive orders</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          "Aggregated and anonymized" means these data are reported only as group statistics
          scoped to a geographic area or demographic segment—never as individual records and never
          tied to your identity. We apply minimum-group-size thresholds and other safeguards to
          prevent re-identification.
        </p>

        <h3>Service providers</h3>
        <p>
          Voxivium engages the following categories of third-party service providers to operate
          the service. Each is bound by contract to process your information only on Voxivium's
          instructions and only for the purposes described in this policy:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Identity verification:</strong> Didit</li>
          <li><strong>Voter registration verification:</strong> Aristotle</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Authentication and push notifications:</strong> Google Firebase
            (Authentication and Cloud Messaging)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Federated sign-in (identity providers):</strong> Google (Sign in with Google)
            and Apple (Sign in with Apple)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Mobile application distribution and in-application purchases:</strong> Apple
            (iOS App Store) and Google (Google Play Store)
          </li>
          <li><strong>Hosting and content delivery:</strong> Cloudflare</li>
          <li><strong>Web analytics:</strong> Cloudflare Web Analytics</li>
          <li><strong>Web payments:</strong> [PAYMENT PROCESSOR]</li>
          <li><strong>Email delivery:</strong> our transactional email provider</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Legal disclosures</h3>
        <p>
          We may disclose information when we are legally required to do so—for example, in
          response to a valid subpoena, court order, or other lawful government request. We will
          challenge requests we believe to be overbroad or unlawful, and where we are not legally
          prohibited from doing so, we will notify the affected user before complying.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
        <p>
          The marketing site does not set tracking cookies. Cloudflare Web Analytics, our
          analytics provider, is cookie-free by design. We use your browser's <code
            >localStorage</code
          > only to remember your color-theme preference, which is not a tracking technology.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Voxivium app uses standard, essential session technologies to keep you signed in.
          These are not used for cross-context advertising or third-party tracking.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Access and correction.</strong> You can view and update your profile data from
            within your account.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Deletion.</strong> You can delete your Voxivium account, and the data
            associated with it, at any time from within the app. Deletion timelines are described
            under "Data retention," below. Our <a href="/legal/delete-account"
              >account deletion page</a
            > gives the step-by-step instructions and itemizes what is deleted and what is kept.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Communication preferences.</strong> You can change which notifications you
            receive at any time. Transactional messages required to operate your account
            (security alerts, billing notices) cannot be disabled while your account remains
            active.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>California residents.</strong> California law gives you specific rights to
            know, access, correct, delete, and limit the use of your personal information, and
            the right not to be discriminated against for exercising those rights. To exercise any
            of these rights, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com"
              >privacy@voxivium.com</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Other U.S. state residents.</strong> Several states grant similar rights. We
            extend the substance of those rights to all U.S. users on request. Contact <a
              href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com">privacy@voxivium.com</a
            >.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain your account data for as long as your account is active. When you delete your
          account—or when we delete it for one of the reasons described below—your account
          information, profile data, identity verification result, voter registration
          verification result, civic input (including belief stances, importance ratings, polling
          responses, and stances on legislation, executive orders, and court rulings), and
          associated records are removed from our production systems within <strong>30 days</strong>
          and are purged from encrypted backups within <strong>90 days</strong>. Aggregated,
          anonymized statistics previously derived from civic input and disclosed to paid
          customers in accordance with this policy are not individually identifiable and are not
          recalled from those customers.
        </p>
        <p>We may delete an account, with or without notice, in the following cases:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The user signs up but does not complete identity verification within a reasonable
            window.
          </li>
          <li>
            The user completes identity verification and is determined to be under 18 years of
            age.
          </li>
          <li>
            The account is dormant or inactive for an extended period, as described in our Terms.
          </li>
          <li>The account is found to be fraudulent or in material breach of our Terms.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may retain limited information for longer where required by law (for example, tax,
          accounting, or fraud-prevention obligations).
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          Voxivium employs administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to protect
          your information, including encryption in transit (TLS) and at rest, scoped access
          controls, audit logging, and periodic security reviews. No method of transmission or
          storage is completely secure, and Voxivium cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>
        <p>
          Personally identifiable information is stored separately from records of your political
          beliefs, which reference an opaque pseudonymous identifier rather than your identity. Our
          <a href="/security">security overview</a> describes this architecture, the standards it is
          engineered against, and how to report a security issue.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Voxivium is restricted to United States citizens who are at least 18 years of age and
          who are registered to vote, and the service is not directed to anyone under 18.
          Voxivium does not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you
          believe a child has provided personal information to Voxivium, contact <a
            href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com">privacy@voxivium.com</a
          > and the information will be deleted.
        </p>

        <h2>Access from outside the United States</h2>
        <p>
          Voxivium operates in the United States, and our servers and service providers are
          located in the United States. Access to Voxivium's account-holder features requires
          verification of identity using a valid United States government-issued photo
          identification and confirmation of active United States voter registration. Eligible
          United States citizens accessing Voxivium from outside the United States are subject to
          the same eligibility and verification requirements as users accessing the service from
          within the United States. By accessing Voxivium from outside the United States, you
          consent to the transfer of your information to, and the processing of your information
          in, the United States, which may have data protection laws that differ from those of
          your location.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Last
          updated" date above and, for material changes, give you advance notice through the
          service or by email. Your continued use of Voxivium after a change takes effect means
          you accept the updated policy.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions, requests to exercise your rights, or any other privacy-related
          inquiries:
        </p>
        <p class="contact">
          <strong>Email:</strong>
          <a href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com">privacy@voxivium.com</a><br />
          <strong>Mail:</strong><br />
          Voxivium, PBC<br />
          921 Pleasant Valley Ave #561<br />
          Mount Laurel, NJ 08054
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

